# Recovery stick

U-Boot on a card that already runs OpenVario loads
`openvario/ov-recovery.itb` from the first FAT partition of the USB
stick. A blank card never looks at USB. The boot ROM only starts the
loader on the SD card.

Build the ramdisk with `bitbake openvario-recovery-image`. The file is
`tmp/deploy/images/${MACHINE}/ov-recovery.itb`.

The stick layout recovery reads is:

```text
openvario/ov-recovery.itb
openvario/images/OV-<version>.img.gz
openvario/upgrade.cfg
```

`upgrade.cfg` is sourced by the shell. A hand-written file needs:

```text
IMAGEFILE=OV-<version>.img.gz
UPGRADE_TYPE=1
```

`IMAGEFILE` is the file name only. Recovery looks it up under
`openvario/images/`. `UPGRADE_TYPE=1` is current firmware to current
firmware and expects partition 3 on the card. After a successful write,
recovery renames `upgrade.cfg` to `_upgrade.cfg`.

The in-system updater also stores brightness, rotation, and service
enablement in that file. Those lines are optional for a stick prepared
by hand.
